# === SMARTENV PROJECT RULES ===

# Language & Standards
- Python 3.8+ compatible. No walrus operator, no match statements.
- Full type hints on every function/class. Must pass mypy --strict.
- Google-style docstrings on every public class and method.
- Zero mandatory runtime dependencies. Cloud/yaml/toml are optional extras.
- All file I/O uses encoding="utf-8" explicitly.
- Thread-safe. No global mutable state. Each Env() instance is isolated.

# Code Style
- Format with black, lint with ruff
- Use conventional commits

# Workflow
- Before implementing, briefly state your plan in 2-3 sentences max.
- After creating a file, run: python -c "import smartenv" to verify no import errors.
- After writing tests, run: python -m pytest tests/ -x -v
- If tests fail, read the error and fix before moving on.
- Update cline_todo.md after completing each task — move items to DONE.
- Be concise. Do not over-explain or pad output with commentary.

# Do NOT
- Do NOT create placeholder or stub files — every file must be complete.
- Do NOT leave "# TODO" comments.
- Do NOT ask me questions — make decisions yourself using best practices.
- Do NOT modify files outside the smartenv/ project directory.